  "reason": "Under Fla. Stat. s. 83.67(6), statutory damages are actual and consequential damages or 3 months' rent, whichever is greater, not 6 months' rent.",
  "verdict": "dispute",
  "issues": [
    "wrong_number_or_date"
  ],
  "proposed_fix": "No. A landlord may not cause, directly or indirectly, the termination or interruption of any utility service furnished to the tenant, whether or not under the landlord's control or paid by the landlord, and may not prevent the tenant from gaining reasonable access to the dwelling unit, such as by changing the locks (Fla. Stat. s. 83.67(1) and (2)). A landlord who violates these provisions is liable for actual and consequential damages or 3 months' rent, whichever is greater, plus costs and attorney's fees (s. 83.67(6))."
